# a key where the old sweep pass ran (TUI-DESIGN-3 §3.6; the owner's directive of 2026-09-23): the committed mark has no idle pass, so a key
# at ≈ 7.5 s after the first frame echoes within the 50 ms max bound and no band frame is ever written (before or after the echo)
expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect step 0/
expect ◆(?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*\d+\.\d+\.\d+
mark settled
expect sess \$
sleep 7.0
mark mid-pass
send h
expect (?:›|>) (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*h
mark echoed
sleep 3.5
mark after
send \x03
expect Say hi
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
